          "source_quote": "οἶμαι δὲ ἐκ τοῦ πλείστου τελευτῆσαι αὐτόν",
          "english_quote": "I think he has most likely died",
          "issue": "ἐκ τοῦ πλείστου is naturally understood here as grounding the inference in the long elapsed time. The draft instead makes it a probability modifier. Its note neither preserves the material temporal alternative nor establishes why “most likely” is preferable; observing that the death is inferred does not distinguish these readings.",
          "suggested_revision": "Propose “I think he has died, given how long it has been,” with a note explaining the implicit temporal reference. If retaining “most likely,” substantiate that lexical reading and disclose the elapsed-time alternative with a contextual rationale. The revised text and note require fresh review; this is an interpretive issue, not evidence of source corruption.",
          "severity": "major"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ καταφιλήσαντες ἦγον ἐπὶ τὴν ξενίαν",
          "english_quote": "embraced us with kisses, and led us to our lodging",
          "issue": "καταφιλήσαντες describes affectionate kissing, not a separate embrace. The English introduces an additional physical gesture. Elsewhere in these passages the source explicitly distinguishes embracing from kissing.",
          "suggested_revision": "Propose “kissed us warmly and led us to our lodging,” without adding an embrace.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
