          "source_quote": "ἢ ἄλλος τις ἐκ φύσεως στοργὴν ἔχων",
          "english_quote": "or anyone else for whom one has natural affection",
          "issue": "The active participle ἔχων makes the other person the holder of the natural affection. The draft reverses that relationship, making the person its recipient and introducing an unspecified “one” as its holder. Reciprocal family affection may be contextually plausible, but it does not justify replacing the source's stated relationship.",
          "suggested_revision": "Propose “or anyone else who feels natural affection,” leaving the affection's object unexpressed as in the Greek.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    },
